{"parentUuid":"9ffdb32e-b674-4d82-b48c-8911ea558d54","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"f5e17534-ecae-4fd2-b53c-7963d9a32666","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"## Today\\nFriday, October 02, 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Knowledge Base\\n\\n319 compiled articles (237 concepts, 81 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here \\u2014 read it only when a question actually needs it:\\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \\\"<query>\\\" --top-k 5`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recent Daily Log\\n\\n\\n**Context:** Evening Mac session \\u2014 ran a full dev-sync across 145 repos, then merged open PRs and moved into Flint (OneDrive catalog triage).\\n\\n**Key Exchanges:**\\n- Asked about the parked AgentAssist PR (#1) while building an AI assistant named Flint. Distinction drawn: Flint *knows* things (thought partner fed by the vault); AgentAssist *does* things (department workflow \\u2014 question ledger routed to TEACH / STUDY / ANSWER). Possible future link: an AgentAssist ledger question could be handed to Flint for a research-backed answer.\\n- Opened the OneDrive import list: 73 folders, 8,994 files, but only **295 files actually held**, sitting in 10 folders. Everything else is already covered by the rules.\\n\\n**Decisions Made:**\\n- Merged **CFB_Analytics_Lab PR #1** (\\\"Lab foundation: data layer, live pull, lesson 0001\\\") \\u2192 `main` at `73d811e`. Eric deleted the `foundation` branch himself (local + remote) after a safety hook blocked the agent.\\n- Left **AgentAssist #1 parked** \\u2014 6 weeks stale, contains out-of-date facts (claims no wellness/sRPE data), and Flint is the focus. Review before any future merge.\\n- Merged **Flint PR #2**: 38 commits of 9/28\\u20139/29 work moved from `step1-triage` to `main` (merge commit `4aa4c6b`). Resolved a `docs/STATUS.md` conflict in favor of the branch; fixed 2 stale lines that falsely claimed the merge was already done.\\n- Did **not** delete `step1-triage` on purpose \\u2014 the Windows laptop has a worktree on that branch holding the only copy of the local book files.\\n- Proposed OneDrive keep/drop sort (pending Eric's accept): keep the 5 `XX_MIGRATION/*` folders + `Conference_Materials` + `APPLIED_PERFORMANCE`; drop personal/HR/photos/video archive; drop `FB_FA24_GPS_SessionReport` (269) and `PracticePlanning` (82) because they hold athlete data, which never goes to Jev.\\n\\n**Lessons Learned:**\\n- **Work stranded on a branch poisons dev-sync.** Flint's `main` read as 9/27 while 38 commits of real work sat on `step1-triage` with no open PR, so the sync reported stale status. Open a PR the same day, or the next sync lies.\\n- **The safety hook blocks compound git commands and all branch deletes.** Splitting into plain single commands works; branch deletion has to be run by Eric.\\n- `sync-to-codex.sh` is not marked executable \\u2014 must be run via `bash <path>`.\\n- Newest-commit-wins is the wrong heuristic for picking a project: graphify-out and CommandCentre had the newest commits but they were only closeout snapshots; PP_Recruiting's 23 commits were the real incoming work.\\n- No new atomizing is possible on the Mac \\u2014 `staging/books`, `ocr`, and `audio` live only on the Windows laptop. Mac sessions are for review and decision work.\\n\\n**Action Items:**\\n- Accept or flip the OneDrive keep/drop sort, then commit + push. Least-certain call: `08_ARCHIVE/PERSONAL` (69 held, 392 papers/books \\u2014 may contain training material).\\n- Verify 2 Flint sources: \\\"The System\\\" and \\\"Black Book Of Secrets\\\".\\n- Then: set the roots \\u2192 skip rules \\u2192 Jev pass on what remains.\\n- Still open from 9/28: Jev blind audit, 3 CLA primer questions, listen to the CVASPS spots.\\n- On Windows next session: in the `step1-triage` worktree, switch to `main`, pull, then delete the branch.\\n- PP_Recruiting: walk Mauro through workbook 017 (UPDATE DATA tab); first decide whether to show OG/OT as-is or trim. Then the 10 honors-benchmark decisions in `docs/2026-09-29-honors-benchmark-plan.md`.\\n- Hook failures surfaced and unresolved: `perch-pull` (exit 1), `daily-backup` (`repo-behind-blocked:global-memory`, `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics`).\\n\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading knowledge base...","durationMs":1127},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4d456b47-0f3d-46fb-acd4-ad72ef582562","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:25:08.977Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"dd4081c0-a71e-46f2-860a-e83f59d2bc85","version":"2.1.287","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"4d456b47-0f3d-46fb-acd4-ad72ef582562","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"f5e17534-ecae-4fd2-b53c-7963d9a32666","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \\\"timeline\\\")\\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\\n       - Each command: {label: \\\"section header\\\", command: \\\"shell command\\\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\\\"q1\\\", \\\"q2\\\", ...])\\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n\\n  <when_not_to_use>\\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\\n  </when_not_to_use>\\n\\n  <file_writing_policy>\\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\\n  </file_writing_policy>\\n\\n  <output_constraints>\\n    <artifact_policy>\\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\\n    </artifact_policy>\\n  </output_constraints>\\n  <session_continuity>\\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\\n  </session_continuity>\\n\\n  <ctx_commands>\\n    \\\"ctx stats\\\" | \\\"ctx-stats\\\" | \\\"/ctx-stats\\\" | context savings question\\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx doctor\\\" | \\\"ctx-doctor\\\" | \\\"/ctx-doctor\\\" | diagnose context-mode\\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx upgrade\\\" | \\\"ctx-upgrade\\\" | \\\"/ctx-upgrade\\\" | update context-mode\\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx purge\\\" | \\\"ctx-purge\\\" | \\\"/ctx-purge\\\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\\n\\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \\\"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\\\"\\n  </ctx_commands>\\n\\n</context_window_protection>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/sessionstart.mjs\"","durationMs":1130},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6d956d8c-f651-4613-babb-7f197cb962ee","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:25:08.981Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"dd4081c0-a71e-46f2-860a-e83f59d2bc85","version":"2.1.287","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"6d956d8c-f651-4613-babb-7f197cb962ee","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\n# User Profile\n\n## About\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\n\n## Preferences\n- Python/R. Two machines: Windows by day, Mac by evening (split 9/24). Tool paths: machine.md.\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\n\n## Working Style\n- Direct; says \"stop\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \"sharpened, not soothed.\"\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\n\n---\n\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\n# Working Memory\n\n## Active Threads\n- **Prioritization slate (9/14)**: LIVE, 5/5. →Tier A prioritization-slate\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: host or local? →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\n- **ATH Tech**: shipped; ITS pending; final run due. →Tier A tech-inventory-refresh\n- **Machine split (9/24)**: Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD. →handoff 2026-09-24-machine-split\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **FB matchups (9/23)**: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py`. →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`\n- **PP Recruiting (9/30)**: 017 sent-ready; 018 (DeJean fix) SHIP. NEXT send 018, walkthrough. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\n- **Sleep sched (9/16)**: R1 merged; NEXT night/early-kickoff. →`sleep-scheduler/`\n- **TypeSafe (9/30)**: triage FAIL 76.5%; Jev>Haiku. PR #31 draft. Video-check prereg drafted, bars pending; Win key saved empty. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`\n- **Flint (9/29)**: Waves 1+2 queued. NEXT Eric: OneDrive keep/drop, 2 verify. →`Flint/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **42Analytics (9/30)**: YouTube channel→Flint. Tier A 122/139 summarized; 12 429-stalled. NEXT finish fetch, verify baseline claims. →`42Analytics/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **PFF DB (9/22)**: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB. →`PFF_Data_Project/docs/`\n\n## Environment Notes\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\n- Win: `Desktop\\DEV` syncs via Drive (robocopy retired 9/22). No large DBs/junctions: renv via `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, PFF via `PFF_DB`.\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\n\n## Pending Decisions\n- **OKR gate (9/14)**: AI buy-in + data governance (Anthony = outside-firm adviser, NOT Mauro). NCAA charter or park?\n\n---\n\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\n\n- **perch-pull** ×1 (2026-10-01 11:55 → 2026-10-01 11:55 UTC): error exit=1 after 3 attempt(s) — see /Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json\n- **daily-backup** ×1 (2026-10-02 01:37 → 2026-10-02 01:37 UTC): 2 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory, manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\n- 1 unparsed line(s); see the file.\n\nFull log: `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Surface this once; clear the file after the user has seen it and the cause is handled.\n\n---\n\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\n\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4310 chars, updated 2026-10-02 11:26)","## Today\nFriday, October 02, 2026\n\n---\n\n## Knowledge Base\n\n319 compiled articles (237 concepts, 81 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here — read it only when a question actually needs it:\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`\n\n---\n\n## Recent Daily Log\n\n\n**Context:** Evening Mac session — ran a full dev-sync across 145 repos, then merged open PRs and moved into Flint (OneDrive catalog triage).\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- Asked about the parked AgentAssist PR (#1) while building an AI assistant named Flint. Distinction drawn: Flint *knows* things (thought partner fed by the vault); AgentAssist *does* things (department workflow — question ledger routed to TEACH / STUDY / ANSWER). Possible future link: an AgentAssist ledger question could be handed to Flint for a research-backed answer.\n- Opened the OneDrive import list: 73 folders, 8,994 files, but only **295 files actually held**, sitting in 10 folders. Everything else is already covered by the rules.\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- Merged **CFB_Analytics_Lab PR #1** (\"Lab foundation: data layer, live pull, lesson 0001\") → `main` at `73d811e`. Eric deleted the `foundation` branch himself (local + remote) after a safety hook blocked the agent.\n- Left **AgentAssist #1 parked** — 6 weeks stale, contains out-of-date facts (claims no wellness/sRPE data), and Flint is the focus. Review before any future merge.\n- Merged **Flint PR #2**: 38 commits of 9/28–9/29 work moved from `step1-triage` to `main` (merge commit `4aa4c6b`). Resolved a `docs/STATUS.md` conflict in favor of the branch; fixed 2 stale lines that falsely claimed the merge was already done.\n- Did **not** delete `step1-triage` on purpose — the Windows laptop has a worktree on that branch holding the only copy of the local book files.\n- Proposed OneDrive keep/drop sort (pending Eric's accept): keep the 5 `XX_MIGRATION/*` folders + `Conference_Materials` + `APPLIED_PERFORMANCE`; drop personal/HR/photos/video archive; drop `FB_FA24_GPS_SessionReport` (269) and `PracticePlanning` (82) because they hold athlete data, which never goes to Jev.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- **Work stranded on a branch poisons dev-sync.** Flint's `main` read as 9/27 while 38 commits of real work sat on `step1-triage` with no open PR, so the sync reported stale status. Open a PR the same day, or the next sync lies.\n- **The safety hook blocks compound git commands and all branch deletes.** Splitting into plain single commands works; branch deletion has to be run by Eric.\n- `sync-to-codex.sh` is not marked executable — must be run via `bash <path>`.\n- Newest-commit-wins is the wrong heuristic for picking a project: graphify-out and CommandCentre had the newest commits but they were only closeout snapshots; PP_Recruiting's 23 commits were the real incoming work.\n- No new atomizing is possible on the Mac — `staging/books`, `ocr`, and `audio` live only on the Windows laptop. Mac sessions are for review and decision work.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Accept or flip the OneDrive keep/drop sort, then commit + push. Least-certain call: `08_ARCHIVE/PERSONAL` (69 held, 392 papers/books — may contain training material).\n- Verify 2 Flint sources: \"The System\" and \"Black Book Of Secrets\".\n- Then: set the roots → skip rules → Jev pass on what remains.\n- Still open from 9/28: Jev blind audit, 3 CLA primer questions, listen to the CVASPS spots.\n- On Windows next session: in the `step1-triage` worktree, switch to `main`, pull, then delete the branch.\n- PP_Recruiting: walk Mauro through workbook 017 (UPDATE DATA tab); first decide whether to show OG/OT as-is or trim. Then the 10 honors-benchmark decisions in `docs/2026-09-29-honors-benchmark-plan.md`.\n- Hook failures surfaced and unresolved: `perch-pull` (exit 1), `daily-backup` (`repo-behind-blocked:global-memory`, `manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics`).\n","\n<context_window_protection>\n  <priority_instructions>\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\n  </priority_instructions>\n\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \"timeline\")\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\n       - Each command: {label: \"section header\", command: \"shell command\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\"q1\", \"q2\", ...])\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\n\n  <when_not_to_use>\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\n  </when_not_to_use>\n\n  <file_writing_policy>\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\n  </file_writing_policy>\n\n  <output_constraints>\n    <artifact_policy>\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\n    </artifact_policy>\n  </output_constraints>\n  <session_continuity>\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\n  </session_continuity>\n\n  <ctx_commands>\n    \"ctx stats\" | \"ctx-stats\" | \"/ctx-stats\" | context savings question\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\n\n    \"ctx doctor\" | \"ctx-doctor\" | \"/ctx-doctor\" | diagnose context-mode\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\n\n    \"ctx upgrade\" | \"ctx-upgrade\" | \"/ctx-upgrade\" | update context-mode\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\n\n    \"ctx purge\" | \"ctx-purge\" | \"/ctx-purge\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\n\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\"\n  </ctx_commands>\n\n</context_window_protection>"],"hookName":"SessionStart","toolUseID":"SessionStart","hookEvent":"SessionStart"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"86a08e7b-8215-41f3-a90e-97be4dbc22d7","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:25:08.983Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nSessionStart hook additional context: ## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\n# User Profile\n\n## About\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\n\n## Preferences\n- Python/R. Two machines: Windows by day, Mac by evening (split 9/24). Tool paths: machine.md.\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\n\n## Working Style\n- Direct; says \"stop\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \"sharpened, not soothed.\"\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\n\n---\n\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\n# Working Memory\n\n## Active Threads\n- **Prioritization slate (9/14)**: LIVE, 5/5. →Tier A prioritization-slate\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: host or local? →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\n- **ATH Tech**: shipped; ITS pending; final run due. →Tier A tech-inventory-refresh\n- **Machine split (9/24)**: Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD. →handoff 2026-09-24-machine-split\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **FB matchups (9/23)**: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py`. →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`\n- **PP Recruiting (9/30)**: 017 sent-ready; 018 (DeJean fix) SHIP. NEXT send 018, walkthrough. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\n- **Sleep sched (9/16)**: R1 merged; NEXT night/early-kickoff. →`sleep-scheduler/`\n- **TypeSafe (9/30)**: triage FAIL 76.5%; Jev>Haiku. PR #31 draft. Video-check prereg drafted, bars pending; Win key saved empty. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`\n- **Flint (9/29)**: Waves 1+2 queued. NEXT Eric: OneDrive keep/drop, 2 verify. →`Flint/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **42Analytics (9/30)**: YouTube channel→Flint. Tier A 122/139 summarized; 12 429-stalled. NEXT finish fetch, verify baseline claims. →`42Analytics/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **PFF DB (9/22)**: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB. →`PFF_Data_Project/docs/`\n\n## Environment Notes\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\n- Win: `Desktop\\DEV` syncs via Drive (robocopy retired 9/22). No large DBs/junctions: renv via `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, PFF via `PFF_DB`.\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\n\n## Pending Decisions\n- **OKR gate (9/14)**: AI buy-in + data governance (Anthony = outside-firm adviser, NOT Mauro). NCAA charter or park?\n\n---\n\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\n\n- **perch-pull** ×1 (2026-10-01 11:55 → 2026-10-01 11:55 UTC): error exit=1 after 3 attempt(s) — see /Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json\n- **daily-backup** ×1 (2026-10-02 01:37 → 2026-10-02 01:37 UTC): 2 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory, manifest-unmanaged:42Analytics - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\n- 1 unparsed line(s); see the file.\n\nFull log: `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Surface this once; clear the file after the user has seen it and the cause is handled.\n\n---\n\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\n\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4310 chars, updated 2026-10-02 11:26)\n## Today\nFriday, October 02, 2026\n\n---\n\n## Knowledge Base\n\n319 compiled articles (237 concepts, 81 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here — read it only when a question actually needs it:\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`\n\n---\n\n## Recent Daily Log\n\n\n**Context:** Evening Mac session — ran a full dev-sync across 145 repos, then merged open PRs and moved into Flint (OneDrive catalog triage).\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- Asked about the parked AgentAssist PR (#1) while building an AI assistant named Flint. Distinction drawn: Flint *knows* things (thought partner fed by the vault); AgentAssist *does* things (department workflow — question ledger routed to TEACH / STUDY / ANSWER). Possible future link: an AgentAssist ledger question could be handed to Flint for a research-backed answer.\n- Opened the OneDrive import list: 73 folders, 8,994 files, but only **295 files actually held**, sitting in 10 folders. Everything else is already covered by the rules.\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- Merged **CFB_Analytics_Lab PR #1** (\"Lab foundation: data l