{"parentUuid":"2470dff2-fd58-4b01-b99d-bacdc48e347b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"86ac494e-5538-47bc-b357-b29aa7d273c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n# AGENTS.md\n\nProject: TypeSafe_Sandbox\n\n## What this is\nA sandbox for building against the TypeSafe System One API (the Jev model), which\nreturns typed judgments and probabilities instead of generated text. The API key is\nNOT stored in this repo; see Secrets below for where it lives on each machine.\n`setup_global_key.sh` installs the macOS side once per machine. `smoke_test.py` proves\nthe key resolves and the API answers.\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n\n## Conventions\n- Durable notes and decisions go in docs/, committed. Not in chat, not in cloud project docs.\n- Documents, data exports, and deliverables live on the primary storage drive (Google Drive 00_Primary_Storage_Drive), not in the repo. Files over 95 MB never go in git.\n- Writing: plain, direct, no em dashes. Documents use the Baylor design system.\n\n## Secrets\n- Never paste the API key into a chat session. Claude Code transcripts under\n  `~/.claude/projects/*.jsonl` are tracked in the `dotclaude` repo and pushed nightly.\n- Never put the key in `~/.claude/settings.json` or `settings.local.json`. Both are tracked.\n(eval):1: ==== not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01712qc77K3hUCT6shAsv4AQ"}]},"uuid":"af8b394d-4a85-4172-87a9-d87453697581","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:28:02.719Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\n# AGENTS.md\n\nProject: TypeSafe_Sandbox\n\n## What this is\nA sandbox for building against the TypeSafe System One API (the Jev model), which\nreturns typed judgments and probabilities instead of generated text. The API key is\nNOT stored in this repo; see Secrets below for where it lives on each machine.\n`setup_global_key.sh` installs the macOS side once per machine. `smoke_test.py` proves\nthe key resolves and the API answers.\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n\n## Conventions\n- Durable notes and decisions go in docs/, committed. Not in chat, not in cloud project docs.\n- Documents, data exports, and deliverables live on the primary storage drive (Google Drive 00_Primary_Storage_Drive), not in the repo. Files over 95 MB never go in git.\n- Writing: plain, direct, no em dashes. Documents use the Baylor design system.\n\n## Secrets\n- Never paste the API key into a chat session. Claude Code transcripts under\n  `~/.claude/projects/*.jsonl` are tracked in the `dotclaude` repo and pushed nightly.\n- Never put the key in `~/.claude/settings.json` or `settings.local.json`. Both are tracked.\n(eval):1: ==== not found","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2470dff2-fd58-4b01-b99d-bacdc48e347b","session_id":"dd4081c0-a71e-46f2-860a-e83f59d2bc85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/TypeSafe_Sandbox","sessionId":"dd4081c0-a71e-46f2-860a-e83f59d2bc85","version":"2.1.287","gitBranch":"main"}
