{"parentUuid":"2efb4671-8264-4324-9892-22c3d0a50132","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"86ac494e-5538-47bc-b357-b29aa7d273c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016XXxJeA2pQGc5hqTAfisYW","type":"tool_result","content":"# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- **2026-10-02 (MAINTENANCE MODE, Eric's call)**: TypeSafe is closed out as an exploration\n  project. Kept and maintained: the skill router, the Zotero classification, and the\n  Research in 5 deliverable verifier. Stopped: hunting for new Jev uses, Spring exit notes (#3),\n  the Jev candidate pick (meeting tagging, study-design classifier, exit-note scoring),\n  `semantic_find` and `autoresearch`. PR #21 was already merged. Draft PR #31 (drive triage, FAIL) and the\n  video-check prereg stay as records; neither gets run further unless Eric reopens them.\n- **2026-10-01 (skill_gate, BUILT, no real runs yet)**: `skill_gate/gate.py` keeps or\n  rejects a rewritten SKILL.md from graded runs of both versions: keep if d > SE, or\n  tied within one SE and cheaper; paired SE when the task sets match. Rule from the\n  Context Language Models paper (arXiv 2609.37725, `clm_icl`); own code, since that repo\n  is CC BY-NC. Stdlib only, no API calls. `test_gate.py` 20/20 planted cases, and four\n  deliberately broken gates (always keep, never pair, ignore cost, forget a dropped task) each fail it.\n  Next, only if wanted: a runner that produces the runs file (headless `claude -p`\n  over a fixed task set plus a grader). No consumer named yet.\n- **2026-10-01 (Windows key verified)**: `smoke_test.py` passes on the Windows laptop\n  (billing question, 0.98). The key in `~/.claude/typesafe.env` is valid (108 chars,\n  `apikey_` prefix) and `typesafe-sdk` 0.7.2 is installed. The same key is now also a\n  Windows user env var (`setx`, same day; smoke test passes with it), so after a Claude Code\n  restart scripts see it with no loading step.\n  Calls can run on Windows now; this supersedes the \"no key or SDK on Windows\" note below.\n- **2026-09-30 (video summary claim check, REGISTERED DRAFT, not run)**: eleventh item.\n  Can Jev flag summary claims a transcript passage does not support? Design copied from\n  `verifier/` (numbers in code, prose to Jev, planted defects as the evidence).\n  Pre-registration `docs/VIDEO_SUMMARY_CHECK_PREREG.md`, sample builder and 100 of 140\n  rows in `video_check/`. **Bars are PROPOSED; Eric approves before any call.** Still to\n-----\n## Next\n- **Watch the shadow log** (`~/.claude/permission-gate/shadow.jsonl`, Windows). After\n  a week or two, count `residue` and look for any real risky call the code rules\n  missed. That is the only evidence left that could reopen a Jev gate. Cheap first\n  win: a v2 `rules.py` (quoted `cd`, `uv run`, `echo` headers, `git -C`, and L1 on\n  path arguments only), pre-registered as a new rule set.\n- **Mac:** copy `permission_gate/{shadow_hook.py,rules.py,sanitize.py}` into\n  `~/.claude/permission-gate/` to turn the shadow hook on there. The settings entry\n  arrives with the dotclaude sync and does nothing until then.\n- **Surgery count, tomorrow:** Eric marks Y/N on the 22 notes in `notes_probe/private/recent_sheet.md`, then `python notes_probe/recent_surgery.py --count`. Put the final figure in `docs/SURGERY_NOTES_PROBE.md` and PR #21; that figure replaces the annual report's 17. Handoff: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-21-surgery-probe-and-12-month-rule.md`.\n- **Cheap retrieval fixes from the rerank measurement** (not Jev): add a\n  \"rewrite the question with the conversation's subject before searching\" line to the\n  `memory-write` retrieval ladder; exclude `dev-docs/TypeSafe_Sandbox/vendor/` from\n  the memsearch index; decide whether `graphify-out/` should be indexed.\n- ~~**`semantic_find` on vendor contracts.**~~ DROPPED. Correction 2026-09-25: there is\n  no Kitman vs Myelin decision and never was. The vendor that came up is Myelin, a\n  startup AMS Baylor is not pursuing; Kitman stays. Nothing to decide, nothing to read.\n- **Find out what wrote `perch.duckdb` on 2026-09-19** (`_INBOX/docs/STATUS.md` says\n  2026-04-30). If the Mac is writing it, the two-writer risk is live now. Then settle\n  box ownership.\n- ~~**Strip reference sections from page text before matching.**~~ DONE 2026-09-20,\n  see Current state. Correction worth keeping: the bibliography was never the cause —\n  removing it alone leaves the band at 37. The in-text `[n]` markers were.\n- **Point the verifier at review 002 and the TOS brief.** The TOS brief is the\n  known-bad case — memory records \"3 misquotes + bad Poisson - DO NOT SEND\" — so if it\n  does not flag those, that is a finding about the verifier, not the brief.\n- ~~**Nothing calls the verifier yet.**~~ WRONG since 2026-09-19: `publish.ps1` in\n  `Weekly_Research_Review` runs it before the Drive copy and refuses on exit 1;\n-----\n## Open questions\n- **API key per machine (moved here from the DEV `PLATFORM.md` router, 2026-09-22):** both machines have a key as of 2026-09-19. Windows is verified end to end against the live API; the Mac key is added but not yet verified. Run `smoke_test.py` on the Mac to close this.\n- ANSWERED 2026-10-02: **Spring exit notes (#3) or maintenance mode? Maintenance.** Eric closed TypeSafe out: router + Zotero classify + verifier kept, no new Jev hunting.\n- ANSWERED 2026-09-20: **governance is no longer a blocker on Jev work.** Eric\n  cleared Option C (\"we can send whatever we need to typesafe\") and separately\n  cleared the Telemetry third-party-processing question. Noted for the record that\n  the Telemetry item was a *vendor contract* question rather than an athlete-privacy\n  one — it binds only if Telemetry-licensed grades go to Jev — and it is cleared\n  either way. Tier labels in `JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md` are now history, not gates.\n- ANSWERED 2026-09-20: **do the Zotero topic renames now? No.** Nothing consumes the\n  labels — they are not written back to Zotero and no workflow reads them. Renaming\n  against no use case is the error that put athlete reconciliation at #2. Revisit\n  when something reads them (a \"what do we have on X\" lookup, or Research in 5 paper\n  selection). Still Eric's, separately: delete the 25 junk records and import the 4\n  TOS papers, both needing a write-access key.\n- ANSWERED 2026-09-20: **athlete reconciliation needs no model, and the capability\n  map's #2 ranking is withdrawn.** Built `athlete_matching/measure_residue.py` (local,\n  no key, no network) over the three systems that have data on this box: Catapult GPS,\n  VALD/ForceDecks, Perch. **Residue = 13 ambiguous pairs.** Of the 300 athletes that\n  found any counterpart above 80, 287 settle on *exact* normalised string equality\n  (693 more scored under 80 and have no counterpart at all) — every settled match\n  scored 100, nothing in the 95–99 band — so fuzzy matching contributes no settled\n  pairs at all. Caveat recorded in the doc: settled means exact-string-equal, **not**\n  confirmed same person; with no DOB, homonyms across seasons are invisible, and that","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9f0ed14c-a52a-4254-9656-5e4a87294727","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:28:06.385Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- **2026-10-02 (MAINTENANCE MODE, Eric's call)**: TypeSafe is closed out as an exploration\n  project. Kept and maintained: the skill router, the Zotero classification, and the\n  Research in 5 deliverable verifier. Stopped: hunting for new Jev uses, Spring exit notes (#3),\n  the Jev candidate pick (meeting tagging, study-design classifier, exit-note scoring),\n  `semantic_find` and `autoresearch`. PR #21 was already merged. Draft PR #31 (drive triage, FAIL) and the\n  video-check prereg stay as records; neither gets run further unless Eric reopens them.\n- **2026-10-01 (skill_gate, BUILT, no real runs yet)**: `skil